# Good Day Sunshine, refrain, first two bars (figure 11.1)
# Pollack's beat row places everything: accents on beats 1 and 4 of the first bar and beat 3 of
# the second (3 + 3 + 2), the F# chord arriving on beat 4 of the first bar.
#? "Day" and "shine" are typed a little after beats 2 and 1; they are placed on the beat.
key A

system
words "Beats"     | 1 2 3 4 | 1 2 3 4 |
words "Accents"   | >*3 > | r*2 >*2 |
# lyrics as typed by Pollack are omitted here; x marks each sung syllable
words "Sung rhythm" | x x*2 x | x*2 x*2 |
chords "Chords"   | B{V-of-V}*3 F#{V-of-(V-of-V)} | - |
